batch guard tests - offline, no quota spent

pacer: ceiling within one process
  first 3 go immediately                                         ok
  4th and 5th are made to wait                                   ok
  counts every request in the day total                          ok

pacer: ceiling ACROSS processes (the reason it is a file)
  all 5 pacer processes exited 0                                 ok
  every child printed one parsable [wait, used, today]           ok
  5 separate processes, 3-rpm ceiling -> 2 had to wait           ok
  the shared counter saw all 5                                   ok

pacer: narrow() only ever lowers the ceiling
  narrow to 8                                                    ok
  narrow to 5 lowers again                                       ok
  narrow to 11 does NOT raise it                                 ok

pacer: a corrupt state file does not stop a batch
  recovers and hands out a slot                                  ok

ledger: the batch cannot spend the live reserve
  batch budget is daily minus reserve                            ok
  one more title still fits at the boundary                      ok
  the title that would overshoot is refused                      ok
  live generation is unaffected by an exhausted batch budget     ok

ledger: asymmetry is deliberate and holds
  live spend eats batch headroom                                 ok
  batch spend does NOT eat the live reserve                      ok
  live generation still allowed after a full batch night         ok

ledger: record() charges the ledger it was told to
  batch charge lands on batch_used                               ok
  live charge lands on live_used                                 ok
  the two counters are independent                               ok

gate: calibrated against the seed set, not guessed
  Helldivers 2 (45.1% veteran, best shape in the eval set) PASSES ok
  Dota 2 (77.0% veteran) is rejected                             ok
  Counter-Strike 2 (61.4%) is rejected, just over the line       ok
  a title with one eligible cohort is rejected outright          ok
  no structure available -> no rejection (fail open, then QR-4 gates) ok

gate: sits on the cost boundary
  filter precedes extract, so the gate sits before the first spend ok
  it reports the measured spend, not a hardcoded zero            ok
  no early return owns the charge any more                       ok

resumability: a restart does not redo settled work
  an existing verdict is skipped                                 ok
  a gate rejection is not re-litigated                           ok
  a crashed title IS retried                                     ok
  an untouched title is queued                                   ok

quota day: rolls at midnight PACIFIC, not midnight UTC
  23:59 PDT (06:59 UTC) is still the previous day                ok
  00:00 PDT (07:00 UTC) starts the new day                       ok
  midnight UTC does NOT roll the quota day                       ok
  23:59 PST (07:59 UTC) is still the previous day                ok
  00:00 PST (08:00 UTC) starts the new day                       ok
  PDT and PST boundaries differ by an hour, so no fixed offset works ok

quota day: both ledgers key on the SAME boundary
  06:59 UTC: live_quota and model_pacer agree (2026-08-01)       ok
  07:00 UTC: live_quota and model_pacer agree (2026-08-02)       ok
  00:30 UTC: live_quota and model_pacer agree (2026-08-01)       ok

quota day: a ledger written before UTC midnight keeps its counters
  the day key written at 00:30 UTC is Aug 1, not Aug 2           ok
  still the same quota day at 06:59 UTC                          ok
  a new quota day only at 07:00 UTC                              ok

