ledger: the pre-flight read of the remote live ledger
  same-day remote live_used is read                              ok
  a remote ledger from another quota day counts 0, not its stale figure ok
  gh missing (rc=127) raises rather than reporting 0             ok
  gh unauthenticated (rc=4) raises rather than reporting 0       ok
  gh timed out (rc=124) raises rather than reporting 0           ok
  output is not JSON raises rather than reporting 0              ok
  output is JSON but not an object raises rather than reporting 0 ok
  ledger has no date raises rather than reporting 0              ok
  live_used is not an int raises rather than reporting 0         ok
  live_used is negative raises rather than reporting 0           ok
  remote higher than local wins                                  ok
  local higher than remote is KEPT - max, not overwrite          ok
  reconcile does not mutate the caller's state                   ok
  folding remote live spend REDUCES batch headroom               ok

ledger: reconciliation survives the loop's re-read
  a fresh load() sees the reconciled live_used, not the old one  ok
  batch_used is untouched by the sync                            ok
  the per-title stop is computed from the reconciled figure      ok
  ...and still allows exactly what remains after it              ok
  re-syncing is idempotent and never lowers live_used            ok
  a live charge after the sync adds to it rather than resetting  ok

ledger: a batch night cannot start blind
  run_batch calls the pre-flight read                            ok
  ...and exits rather than continuing when it raises             ok
  ...guarded by an explicit opt-out flag, not silent             ok
  run_batch PERSISTS the reconciled figure rather than merging in memory ok
  ...and the loop's stop really does re-read from disk, which is why ok
  the persisted state is what the startup budget is computed from ok
  no code path substitutes 0 for an unreadable ledger            ok

